{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "UOKoZvWElp", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-24", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 918824, "segment_id": "6UeToC9qV6", "segment_broadcast_id": "UOKoZvWElp", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Katie Couric (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 918824, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "UOKoZvWElp", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-24", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 918824, "segment_id": "x4DmpN7biv", "segment_broadcast_id": "UOKoZvWElp", "segment_title": "Campaign 2008 / Obama vs. McCain / The Economy / McCain Interview ", "segment_description": "(Studio: Katie Couric) Report introduced.  \n\n(New York: Chip Reid) The response of presidential candidates Senators John McCain and Barack Obama to the economic crisis featured; details given of McCain's suspension of his campaign to work on the bailout plan, his call to postpone Friday\u2019s debate and Obama\u2019s phone call to McCain to propose a joint statement. [McCAIN \u2013 calls for the president to convene a leadership meeting.] [OBAMA \u2013 says the people need to hear from the person who will be responsible for dealing with this mess.]  \n\n(Studio: Katie Couric) Exclusive interview held with McCain about his actions. [McCAIN \u2013 says at this time we can\u2019t worry about politics; says it\u2019s not time for statements, it is time to act; talks about the seriousness of the crisis; comments on whether the debate subject should be changed to the economy; reacts to Governor Sarah Palin\u2019s warning about a depression; comments on what the people need to hear; says America\u2019s best days are still ahead; comments on reaction to the bailout plan.] Obama\u2019s inability to appear on the broadcast due to a schedule and his news conference to address the financial crisis noted. [In Tampa, OBAMA \u2013 comments on the miscommunication over the timing of the joint statement and McCain\u2019s announcement; says he talks to Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson every day; says it is part of the president\u2019s job to deal with more than one thing at once and we should have the debate.] ", "segment_duration": 510, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 918825, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "UOKoZvWElp", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-24", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 918824, "segment_id": "csBRsmJv2K", "segment_broadcast_id": "UOKoZvWElp", "segment_title": "Economy: Financial Crisis / Bailout Plan", "segment_description": "(Studio: Katie Couric) President Bush's plan to address the nation tonight to push the bailout plan for the economy noted.   (Washington: Bob Orr) The battle over the bailout featured; scenes shown of several Congressmembers commenting on taxpayer anger; details given of agreements on oversight and executive compensation and negotiations on equity stakes and foreclosures. [Federal Reserve Board chairman Ben BERNANKE \u2013 says this is the most significant financial crisis in the post-war period.] [Representative John BOEHNER&#134;- says Congress has a responsibility to act.] [Treasury Secretary Henry PAULSON \u2013 comments on the compensation issue.]   (Studio: Katie Couric) Coverage of Bush\u2019s speech noted. ", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63560.0", "legacy_segment_id": 918826, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "UOKoZvWElp", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-24", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 918824, "segment_id": "3mN84UCpLN", "segment_broadcast_id": "UOKoZvWElp", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Katie Couric) Stock Market Report", "segment_description": " ", "segment_duration": 20, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63710.0", "legacy_segment_id": 918827, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "UOKoZvWElp", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-24", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1710, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 918824, "segment_id": "CsQeQLrIdO", "segment_broadcast_id": "UOKoZvWElp", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Healthy Choice; Reclast; Zantac; \u201cBody of Lies\u201d; Swanson.)", "segment_description": " ", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63730.0", "legacy_segment_id": 918828, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_